+/// Sweep this dynamic body against sweep targets alone (b3Body_SetSweepTarget), in place of its continuous collision
+/// against static bodies, whether that is enabled or not. Off by default. When it moves fast enough for continuous
+/// collision, and the world's is enabled, it is swept once the broad-phase is refit, as a bullet is, from the pose it
+/// began the step in to the one it ends it in, against the kinematic and dynamic targets near it. With no target near
+/// it nothing changes: its bounds and contacts are those of a body that is not swept. A hit puts it back to the time
+/// of impact, as continuous collision does, keeping its velocity. For a body that must not pass through thin shapes
+/// that move, such as a car meeting posts that yield, where sweeping it against everything would cost too much or
+/// catch it on the ground it rolls over.
+B3_API void b3Body_SetSweepTargetsOnly( b3BodyId bodyId, bool flag );
+
+/// Is this body swept against sweep targets alone?
+B3_API bool b3Body_IsSweepTargetsOnly( b3BodyId bodyId );
+
+/// Make this body a target of the bodies swept against sweep targets alone (b3Body_SetSweepTargetsOnly). Off by
+/// default. Only a kinematic or dynamic target is seen, never a bullet or a body swept against targets itself.
+B3_API void b3Body_SetSweepTarget( b3BodyId bodyId, bool flag );
+
+/// Is this body a sweep target?
+B3_API bool b3Body_IsSweepTarget( b3BodyId bodyId );
+
 /// Allow this body to rotate fast. Useful for axially symmetric bodies, such as vehicle wheels.
 /// Normally rotation speed is clamped to improve CCD. However, this clamping is unnecessary for
 /// bodies that only rotate fast around an axis of symmetry.
